FerrionOS change to upstream userutils (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 641a5aa81574db79d883151bc3438d3e59f90b88 after the existing recipe patches.

One password: login and the new unlock-session command (for the graphical login) start the first session of the account whose key slot opened the volume at startup without a password, once per boot, reading the slot from /scheme/sys/env and the account from the root-only /etc/unlock-slots, never after a recovery-key unlock. The once-per-boot claim is tracked through UnlockState and stored inside /var/run/unlock-session (root-owned, mode 0700, created and cleared at boot by 00_unlock_claim), refusing symlinks and failing closed when the directory is missing or has group or other permissions. Every key-slot caller maps redoxfs-key's exit status into KeyOutcome (Applied, Unchanged, Unknown), keeping the invariant that no live disk slot of an account exists without a record in /etc/unlock-slots: passwd saves the new login password whenever the disk slot change applied, passwd --enroll records any applied or uncleaned unknown slot so userdel can revoke it, and userdel revokes the disk slot (idempotently accepting an already-clear slot) before removing the record from /etc/unlock-slots.

